+### 1.4 A Length mapping for a group of six or more — `patches/fixes/0002-length-group-of-six-or-more.patch`
+
+Also in the second patch group, and also a send to `#f`. The Slipnet has Length
+nodes for 1 to 5 only (`*slipnet-numbers*`), so `number->platonic-number`
+(`slipnet.ss:495`) returns `#f` for a group of six or more objects, and that
+group's `platonic-length` is `#f` (`groups.ss:86`). `attach-length-description`
+(`groups.ss:836-844`) already allows for it ("Check for groups longer than five
+objects"): such a group gets no Length description.
+
+- **`build-bridge`** (`bridges.ss:1396-1411`), for a horizontal bridge, made a Length
+  concept-mapping whenever the two objects' platonic lengths differ. With a letter
+  or a shorter group on one side and a group of six or more on the other, the
+  `#f` reached `make-concept-mapping`, whose `get-CM-short-name` was sent to it
+  (`concept-mappings.ss:40`): "attempt to apply non-procedure #f". The mapping is
+  now made only when both lengths exist, as the Length description is.
+
+**Effect on behaviour: none where it does not fire.** The send always crashed
+when it arose (`aaa -> aaaaaa; aaa`, seed 1, at codelet 608). When both objects
+are groups of six or more the lengths are equal (both `#f`), no mapping was made
+before and none is now.
+
